experiment: orthoname
  instrument        orthoname   trial seed 000000000135206e   1214 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `orthovocab` showed two SEQUENTIAL lessons on different
                    axes coexist (77% less damage, 10.7 SE). Naming is
                    SIMULTANEOUS and conditional. Does spreading a vocabulary
                    across articulators make the milestone reachable?
  the encodings     collide: both words move F1, opposite ways.
                    ortho:   one word moves F1, the other F2.
                    MATCHED on target separation (0.58 log units both), so
                    neither is handed the score. ortho pays 1.41x more per
                    lesson, which works against the hypothesis.
  the control       matched marginal per encoding: same targets, same reward
                    rate, conditionality removed. Contexts ON in every arm.
  the refusal       neither beating its own control means naming did not
                    happen at all; ortho not beating collide means the
                    sequential result does not transfer. 36 seeds.


  arm           margin (log units)     nearest-target fraction
  collide       +0.1747 +/- 0.0000        0.958
  collide-rnd   -0.0197 +/- 0.0000        0.389
  ortho         +0.0969 +/- 0.0000        0.958
  ortho-rnd     +0.0011 +/- 0.0000        0.542

  ARM LIVENESS vs `collide` (seeds where the arm differs at all)
    collide-rnd        36/36
    ortho              36/36
    ortho-rnd          36/36

  EXCESS over each encoding's OWN matched marginal, paired on seed.
  This is what CONDITIONALITY bought, with the targets held fixed.
    collide  +0.1944 +/- 0.0119  (+16.3 SE)
    ortho    +0.0958 +/- 0.0060  (+15.8 SE)
    ortho - collide  -0.0986 +/- 0.0117  (-8.4 SE)  [paired]

  THE VOCABULARY IS NOT THE PROBLEM (-8.4 SE). An orthogonal encoding does
  not name better than a colliding one, so `orthovocab`'s result is a fact
  about SEQUENTIAL lessons that does not transfer to simultaneous conditional
  ones. Interference between lessons taught one after another, and the
  failure to condition on the heard word, are different problems -- and this
  run says only the first is about sharing a dimension.
